│ Cross-referencing architecture:
- Every factual claim carries [Ref: XX-§Y] notation where XX = meso-artifact number, §Y = section within that artifact
- Inter-cluster references use [→ Cluster X, §Y] notation
- FENNEXT-derived implications are marked as [FENNEXT-IMP] to distinguish from source-extracted facts
- Regulatory anchors carry full citation (KMS Nr. X, Datum, Az.)

Structural convention for all clusters:
1. ZWECK — one sentence, what this cluster answers
2. KERNREGELN / KERNLOGIK — the operational content
3. FENNEXT-IMPLIKATIONEN — pre-computed strategic derivations
4. QUELLVERWEISE — meso-artifact traceability

This architecture ensures:
- Future sessions can load ONE cluster for a specific task without needing all four
- No information duplication between clusters (only cross-references)
- Implications are pre-computed, not re-derived each session
- Regulatory traceability survives any number of derivation layers   │
